    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d113-a2">

                <pb facs="0203" n="129" sameAs="frus:frus1866p1/pg129"/>

                <head>Mr. Hull to Mr. Bateson.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>No. 6 <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cook Street</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Liverpool,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1866-01-30"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >January</hi> 30, 1866.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Sir:</hi> Messrs. Fraser, Trenholm &amp; Co
                    instruct us to inform you that they never paid her Margaret Marshall or any
                    other wife, of any seaman of the Shenandoah, a sixpence any time.</p>
                <p>Their name has, no doubt, been put into the mouth of an ignorant woman by the
                    zealous detective who supplies information to the American consul.</p>
                <p>Yours, truly,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>F. S. HULL.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">W. G. Bateson,</hi> Esq.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
